PARITY reproduced exactly from the web source (cross-platform behavior parity)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  vehicle label = v.display_name || v.vin || `Vehicle ${v.id}`        (null-safe fallback chain)
  window opts   = ALL_WINDOWS.map → label = t(`admin.xray.windowOption.${w}`, w) [token fallback]
  bucket opts   = ALL_BUCKETS.map → label = t(`admin.xray.bucketOption.${b}`, b) [token fallback]
  bucket disable= tooBig = BUCKET_SECS[b] >= WINDOW_SECS[windowSel]   (avoids server 400)
                  WINDOW_SECS {5m:300,15m:900,1h:3600,6h:21600,24h:86400}
                  BUCKET_SECS {30s:30,1m:60,5m:300,15m:900,1h:3600}
  controlled    = onVehicleChange / onWindowChange / onBucketChange forwarded via a change sink;
                  setWindow does NOT auto-correct the bucket (faithful to the web component).
  i18n keys     = admin.xray.controls.selectVehicle/vehicleAria/windowAria/bucketAria +
                  admin.xray.windowOption.{5m,15m,1h,6h,24h} + admin.xray.bucketOption.{30s,1m,5m,15m,1h}
                  (the 4 prompt-listed strings + the full ALL_WINDOWS/ALL_BUCKETS option keys).

States reproduced (every one renders — no hidden surfaces), each with a #if DEBUG preview:
  loading (skeleton row) · content (3 pickers) · empty (hint + still-usable window/bucket) ·
  error (retry) · stale (chip + banner + one auto-refresh) · offline (cached + chip + banner).

